cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Sema in your research or build on the pattern vocabulary,
  please cite the preprint below. If you are citing the software
  itself rather than the underlying ideas, the metadata at the top of
  this file is also valid as a software citation.
title: "Sema: Content-Addressed Semantics for Multi-Agent Coordination"
abstract: >-
  Sema is a semantic commons that content-addresses meaning itself:
  the definition is the identifier. By deriving identifiers from the
  cryptographic hash of a pattern's definition, any divergence in
  meaning produces a distinct hash, guaranteeing that misaligned
  agents halt rather than fail silently.
authors:
  - family-names: Westerberg
    given-names: Henrik
type: software
url: "https://semahash.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/emergent-wisdom/sema"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - multi-agent-systems
  - alignment
  - content-addressing
  - semantic-coordination
  - knowledge-graph
  - mcp
